## Expected Results

The query may identify activity such as:

```text
powershell.exe -EncodedCommand SQBFAFgA...
```

```text
pwsh.exe -ec SQBFAFgA...
```

```text
powershell.exe -Command IEX(...)
```

```text
powershell.exe -Command [Convert]::FromBase64String(...)
```

```text
powershell.exe -Command ([char]65,[char]66,[char]67)-join ''
```

```text
powershell.exe -Command $Value -bxor 35
```

Results should be reviewed alongside:

- The parent process
- The complete command line
- The user account
- The device
- Subsequent child processes
- Related network and file activity

---

## Potential False Positives

Legitimate results may include:

- Administrative automation
- Software deployment
- Device-management platforms
- Security products
- Approved maintenance scripts
- Penetration testing
- Red-team activity
- Complex PowerShell scripts using compression or encoding

Known legitimate scripts and command-line patterns may be excluded after they have been reviewed.

---

## Limitations

This query does not prove that an encoded or obfuscated command is malicious.

It may also miss:

- PowerShell launched through a renamed executable
- Obfuscation techniques not included in the query
- Obfuscation contained inside a script file
- Commands where the encoded payload is constructed at runtime
- Encoded-command abbreviations not covered by the regular expression
- PowerShell activity without visible process command-line telemetry

The query extracts potential encoded content but does not attempt to decode it.

PowerShell encoded commands are commonly created from Unicode text before being converted to Base64, so decoding them correctly requires the appropriate character encoding.

